spaced every other cell rightward from the key pixel.\n0019: \n0020:     Key insight: The legend is both the color index and the output canvas — object counts become dot sequences on the matching row.\n0021:     \"\"\"\n0022:     g = np.array(grid, dtype=int)\n0023:     H, W = g.shape\n0024:     _bg = int(get_bg(g))\n0025: \n0026:     black = 0\n0027: \n0028:     # STEP 1) Find the legend bbox: largest black CC whose bbox contains some non-black pixels.\n0029:     best = None  # (area, bbox)\n0030:     for coords in components_mask(g == int(black), connectivity=8):\n0031:         if coords.size == 0:\n0032:             continue\n0033:         b = bbox_coords(coords)\n0034:         sub = crop_bbox(g, b)\n0035:         if (sub != int(black)).any():\n0036:             area = int(coords.shape[0])\n0037:             cand = (area, tuple(map(int, b)))\n0038:             if best is None or cand[0] > best[0]:\n0039:                 best = cand\n0040: \n0041:     assert not (best is None)\n0042: \n0043:     r0, c0, r1, c1 = map(int, best[1])\n0044:     box = crop_bbox(g, (r0, c0, r1, c1))\n0045:     bh, bw = map(int, box.shape)\n0046: \n0047:     # STEP 2) Inside the legend bbox, find the key column:\n0048:     # leftmost column with any non-black pixels (the \"key pixels\").\n0049:     key_col = None\n0050:     for cc in range(bw):\n0051:         if (box[:, int(cc)] != int(black)).any():\n0052:             key_col = int(cc)\n0053:             break\n0054:     if key_col is None:\n0055:         return np.zeros_like(box)\n0056: \n0057:     keys = [(int(rr), int(box[int(rr), int(key_col)])) for rr in range(bh) if int(box[int(rr), int(key_col)]) != int(black)]\n0058:     keys.sort(key=lambda t: int(t[0]))\n0059: \n0060:     outside = np.ones((H, W), dtype=bool)\n0061:     outside[int(r0) : int(r1) + 1, int(c0) : int(c1) + 1] = False\n0062:     out = np.zeros((bh, bw), dtype=int)\n0063: \n0064:     # STEP 3/4) Count CCs of each key color outside the legend, then draw 1 dot per CC.\n0065:     for rr, col in keys:\n0066:         mask = (g == int(col)) & outside\n0067:         _labc, nc = label_mask(mask, connectivity=8)\n0068:         for i in range(int(nc)):\n0069:             cc = int(key_col + 2 * i)\n0070:             if 0 <= cc < bw:\n0071:                 out[int(rr), int(cc)] = int(col)\n0072: \n0073:     return out\n0074: \n0075: # --------------- generator (o5x) ---------------\n0076: \n0077: # Palette and legend color choices.\n0078: COLOR_POOL = tuple(range(1, 10))\n0079: BLACK = 0\n0080: DISTRACTOR_PROB = 0.5\n0081: \n0082: # Key rows and tally dimensions.\n0083: KEY_COUNT_RANGE = (2, 4)\n0084: TARGET_COUNT_RANGE = (1, 5)\n0085: KEY_ROW_FIRST = 1\n0086: KEY_ROW_STEP = 2\n0087: KEY_COLUMN = 1\n0088: TALLY_COL_STEP = 2\n0089: LEGEND_HEIGHT_TAIL = 1\n0090: LEGEND_WIDTH_TAIL = 1\n0091: LEGEND_SLACK_RANGE = (0, 3)\n0092: \n0093: # Canvas size and legend placement bounds.\n0094: GRID_HEIGHT_RANGE = (20, 25)\n0095: GRID_WIDTH_RANGE = (20, 25)\n0096: LEGEND_EDGE_MARGIN = 2\n0097: \n0098: # Sprite shape and placement constraints.\n0099: SPRITE_AREA_RANGE = (4, 7)\n0100: SPRITE_BBOXES = ((2, 2), (2, 3), (3, 2), (3, 3))\n0101: SPRITE_CONNECTIVITY = 8\n0102: SPRITE_PADDING = 1\n0103: SPRITE_PADDING_CONNECTIVITY = 8\n0104: \n0105: # Retry budget for rejection sampling.\n0106: GENERATION_ATTEMPTS = 300\n0107: \n0108: \n0265: def generate_input() -> np.ndarray:\n0266:     for _ in range(GENERATION_ATTEMPTS):\n0267:         grid = _gen_attempt()\n0268:         if grid is not None:\n0269:             return grid\n0270:     raise RuntimeError(\"failed to generate a valid 58490d8a input\")\n\n===== /home/lixinyu/snap/new/ARC_code/train/ad38a9d0.py =====\n0022: def main(grid: np.ndarray) -> np.ndarray:\n0023:     \"\"\"Recolor each placeholder object according to its normalized shape while leaving the background fixed.\n0024: \n0025:     Input structure\n0026:     A same-size grid with one dominant background color and one foreground\n0027:     placeholder color forming separated 4-connected objects.\n0028: \n0029:     Rule\n0030:     Replace every placeholder object by the color assigned to its exact\n0031:     translation-normalized mask; all background pixels remain unchanged.\n0032: \n0033:     Key insight\n0034:     The input objects are a shape legend with repeated instances: identical\n0035:     masks always receive identical colors, independent of their position.\n0036:     \"\"\"\n0037:     g = np.asarray(grid, dtype=int)\n0038:     bg = get_bg(g)\n0039:     fg_colors = colors_present(g, exclude={bg})\n0040:     assert len(fg_colors) == 1\n0041: \n0042:     out = g.copy()\n0043:     comps = find_components(\n0044:         g,\n0045:         bg=bg,\n0046:         colors=[fg_colors[0]],\n0047:         connectivity=4,\n0048:         monochromatic=True,\n0049:     )\n0050:     assert comps\n0051:     for comp in comps:\n0052:         coords = comp[\"coords\"]\n0053:         shape = _shape_signature(coords)\n0054:         assert shape in SHAPE_TO_COLOR\n0055:         out[tuple(coords.T)] = SHAPE_TO_COLOR[shape]\n0056:     return out\n0057: \n0058: # --------------- generator (att1) ---------------\n0059: \n0060: # Canvas and colors.\n0061: GRID_H = 9\n0062: GRID_W = 9\n0063: BG_COLOR = 7\n0064: FG_COLOR = 6\n0065: \n0066: # Object count and retry limits.\n0067: MIN_OBJECTS = 6\n0068: MAX_OBJECTS_EXCLUSIVE = 9\n0069: GENERATION_RETRIES = 300\n0070: RESERVED_PADDING = 1\n0071: \n0072: # Canonical shapes: (cells, height, width), in the same order used for duplicates.\n0073: SHAPES = [\n0074:     (((0, 0), (0, 1), (1, 1)), 2, 2),  # L-triomino -> 4\n0075:     (((0, 0), (0, 1), (1, 1), (1, 2)), 2, 3),  # S-tetromino -> 8\n0076:     (((0, 1), (1, 0), (1, 1), (1, 2), (2, 1)), 3, 3),  # plus -> 3\n0077:     (((0, 0), (1, 0), (2, 0)), 3, 1),  # vertical-3 -> 2\n0078:     (((0, 0), (1, 0)), 2, 1),  # domino -> 9\n0079:     (((0, 0), (0, 1), (0, 2), (1, 0), (1, 1), (1, 2)), 2, 3),  # 2x3 rect -> 5\n0080: ]\n0081: \n0082: \n0140: def generate_input():\n0141:     for _ in range(GENERATION_RETRIES):\n0142:         result = _gen_attempt()\n0143:         if result is not None:\n0144:             return result\n0145:     raise RuntimeError(f\"Failed to generate input after {GENERATION_RETRIES} attempts\")\n\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
